My first roguelike was Sword of Fargoal on the VIC-20.  I suppose I betray a 
bit of age when I write this :-/ It was written and distributed in the 
rather brain-dead BASIC that the old Commodores had, and I even managed 
some patches -- a pause function and later a port of the VIC-20 code to the 
C64.

That pause function was particularly critical, because while there was no 
equivalent to You Know Who, once you found the Sword of Fargoal you had 
about 30 minutes *real time* to get the hell out of the dungeon.  But a 
teenager's life seldom has such time interrupted -- one must constantly 
deal with the parents' demands on his time.

I still have that C64, and maybe the port might still be readable on one of 
the dozens of 5.25" floppies that I still have from those days, and it 
might be interesting, if I can recover it, to compare that port to the 
official C64 version.


